Vietnam
The Jimny was launched in Vietnam on 10 April 2024, in the sole variant, paired only with a 4-speed automatic.&#91;88&#93;

Europe[edit]
The Jimny made its European debut starting in Germany in October 2018.&#91;89&#93;&#91;90&#93;
In 2020, the Jimny was discontinued from European markets due to its high carbon dioxide emissions and stringent European emission standards. It was reintroduced in the middle of 2021 as a commercial vehicle that is subjected to less stringent European emissions standards, with the rear seats removed and a partition separates the boot space from the front seats.&#91;91&#93;
In June 2025, the Jimny was discontinued in most European markets due to tougher emission standards and there were no immediate plans for the Jimny to use battery electric powertrains.&#91;92&#93;

GCC[edit]
The Jimny 3-door was launched in the GCC markets in February 2021, it is available in two trim levels, GL (with manual) and GLX (with automatic).&#91;93&#93;
